9) app/Providers/ - Providers participate in Laravel's bootstrapping process.

		A Service Provider tells Laravel how to register or initialize a service.

		app/Providers/
		       ↓
		Service Provider classes
		       ↓
		register()
		       ↓
		Service Container
		       ↓
		boot()
		       ↓
		Application ready

		A Service Provider is a class Laravel uses to register and/or initialize services in the application, and app/Providers/ is where your application's provider classes live.

		There are two important methods:
		register() - register() is mainly used to register things into Laravel's Service Container.

		public function register()
		{
		    $this->app->singleton(PaymentService::class, function ($app) {
			return new PaymentService();
		    });
		}

		boot() - 
		register()
		    ↓
		Tell Laravel about services

		boot()
		    ↓
		Initialize/configure things after registration

i)Service Container- The Service Container is a Laravel system responsible for creating and resolving objects/services.

		$payment = app(PaymentService::class);

		app(PaymentService::class)
			    ↓
		    Service Container
			    ↓
		"How do I create PaymentService?"
			    ↓
		new PaymentService()
			    ↓
		PaymentService object

		So the container is essentially a place where Laravel can resolve dependencies and construct objects.

ii)Dependency Injection - 
			Now suppose OrderService needs PaymentService.

			Without dependency injection:
			class OrderService
			{
			    public function createOrder()
			    {
				$payment = new PaymentService();

				$payment->charge();
			    }
			}

			OrderService is manually creating its dependency.

			With Dependency Injection:

			class OrderService
			{
			    public function __construct(
				PaymentService $payment
			    ) {
				$this->payment = $payment;
			    }
			}
			Dependency Injection means giving an object the dependencies it needs instead of making the object create those dependencies itself.

iii)Service Providers - 
		A Service Provider is commonly where you tell Laravel's container about your application's services.
		class AppServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
		{
