		vi)scoped dependencies - 
		A scoped binding is similar to a singleton, but its lifetime is limited to a particular application/request lifecycle.
		Conceptually:
		Request #1
		    ↓
		PaymentService instance A

		Request #2
		    ↓
		PaymentService instance B

		Within Request #1:
		resolve PaymentService
		       ↓
		same instance

		But when the next request/lifecycle begins:
		new lifecycle
		       ↓
		new instance

		The important distinction:
		bind
		    ↓
		new instance as needed

		singleton
		    ↓
		one shared instance for the container/application lifetime

		scoped
		    ↓
		one instance per lifecycle/request scope

